- Follow the original task names and order exactly.
- Only fix linting issues reported; do not alter the functional intent or add/remove tasks.
- Output must consist solely of the corrected YAML playbook.

Inputs:
- Original generation prompt:
Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.  
The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).  
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.  

Task 1: Import assert.yml
Description Task 1: Import assertion tasks from assert.yml file for validation checks. Run once on localhost.

Task 2: Install apache httpd
Description Task 2: Install Apache HTTPD packages specified in httpd_packages variable.

Task 3: Configure selinux
Description Task 3: Configure SELinux settings if it is enabled. Modify SELinux boolean settings in httpd_sebooleans and allow connections on specified ports (httpd_port and httpd_ssl_port).

Task 4: Configure httpd
Description Task 4: Configure Apache HTTPD by templating configuration file from httpd_config_src to httpd_config_dest with mode 0644. Notify handlers for configuration test and service restart.

Task 5: Activate httpd module | Debian
Description Task 5: Activate Apache HTTPD modules using a2enmod command for Debian-based systems. Loop through httpd_modules_to_activate_with_command.

Task 6: Import ssl.yml
Description Task 6: Import SSL configuration tasks from ssl.yml when https_ssl_enable is true.

Task 7: Import locations.yml
Description Task 7: Import locations configuration tasks from locations.yml when httpd_locations is defined.

Task 8: Import vhosts.yml
Description Task 8: Import virtual hosts configuration tasks from vhosts.yml when httpd_vhosts is defined.

Task 9: Configure ports
Description Task 9: Configure Apache HTTPD ports by templating ports configuration file. Notify handlers for configuration test and service restart. Only for Debian and Suse systems.

Task 10: Import directories.yml
Description Task 10: Import directories configuration tasks from directories.yml when httpd_directories is defined.

Task 11: Flush handlers
Description Task 11: Flush all registered handlers to execute them immediately.

Task 12: Removing default html
Description Task 12: Remove default HTML file from httpd_data_directory if httpd_remove_example is true.

Task 13: Start and enable httpd
Description Task 13: Start and enable Apache HTTPD service named httpd_service.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook:
---
- name: Import assert.yml
  ansible.builtin.import_tasks: assert.yml
  delegate_to: localhost
  run_once: true

- name: Install apache httpd
  ansible.builtin.package:
    name: "{{ httpd_packages }}"
    state: present

- name: Configure selinux
  ansible.posix.selinux:
    state: targeted
    policy: targeted
    booleans: "{{ httpd_sebooleans }}"
  when: ansible_selinux_enabled

- name: Configure httpd
  ansible.builtin.template:
    src: "{{ httpd_config_src }}"
    dest: "{{ httpd_config_dest }}"
    mode: "0644"
  notify:
    - configuration test
    - service restart

- name: Activate httpd module | Debian
  ansible.builtin.command: a2enmod "{{ item }}"
  with_items: "{{ httpd_modules_to_activate_with_command }}"
  when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"

- name: Import ssl.yml
  ansible.builtin.import_tasks: ssl.yml
  when: https_ssl_enable

- name: Import locations.yml
  ansible.builtin.import_tasks: locations.yml
  when: httpd_locations is defined

- name: Import vhosts.yml
  ansible.builtin.import_tasks: vhosts.yml
  when: httpd_vhosts is defined

- name: Configure ports
  ansible.builtin.template:
    src: ports.conf.j2
    dest: "{{ httpd_ports_file }}"
    mode: "0644"
  notify:
    - configuration test
    - service restart
  when: ansible_os_family in ["Debian", "Suse"]

- name: Import directories.yml
  ansible.builtin.import_tasks: directories.yml
  when: httpd_directories is defined

- name: Flush handlers
  ansible.builtin.meta: flush_handlers

- name: Removing default html
  ansible.builtin.file:
    path: "{{ httpd_data_directory }}/index.html"
    state: absent
  when: httpd_remove_example

- name: Start and enable httpd
  ansible.builtin.service:
    name: "{{ httpd_service }}"
    state: started
    enabled: true


